  "bio": "A hadith scholar from Harran who settled in Egypt and died there in 229; al-Bukhari heard him in several places (the Zahrat al-Muta'allimin counts twenty-three hadith), and Ibn Majah is the only other of the six to use him. Counted an Egyptian by residence, which is what makes the chain of hadith 12 Egyptian from top to bottom. His sons Muhammad and Ali transmitted from him, and his copying for Abu Salih al-Harrani is recorded.",
